//
// Overlays that would load and then misbehave must be refused at build time.
//
// Everything here shares a character: it produces a program that links, loads,
// and then does something subtly wrong. None of it is caught by the compiler,
// and none of it looks like a failure at run time -- which is exactly why the
// checks have to exist and have to be tested.
//
// This is also the "very long llvm-aie-generated program memory" case: the
// overlay is a Peano-compiled object whose .text is sized exactly, so the slot
// boundary can be tested at the boundary rather than near it.
//
// REQUIRES: peano
//
// RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
// RUN: %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR/bin/clang++ --target=aie2p-none-unknown-elf -O2 -c %S/../resident.cc -o %t/resident.o
// RUN: %python %S/../pm.py emit --recipe one_slot --slot-ld %t/slot.ld --phases 0 --out %t/d1.mlir
// RUN: cd %t && %aiecc --tmpdir=%t/p1 --get-xclbin --xclbin-name=%t/p1.xclbin --get-npu-insts --npu-insts-name=%t/p1.bin %t/d1.mlir
//
// Exactly slot-sized is legal: the boundary is inclusive, and a test that only
// ever checked "well under" would not notice it moving.
// RUN: %python %S/../pm.py workload --tag 1 --size 0x2000 --output %t/full.o --workdir %t
// RUN: %python %S/../pm.py link --object %t/full.o --resident %t/p1 --recipe one_slot --output %t/full.elf | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FULL
// FULL: full.elf: 8192 bytes at 0x2000
//
// One padding block over, and the write would run past the slot. 0x2020 rather
// than 0x2010 because padding comes in 32-byte blocks: asking for a size off
// that grid is refused with the two reachable neighbours, which is the right
// behaviour but not what this line is testing.
// RUN: %python %S/../pm.py workload --tag 2 --size 0x2020 --output %t/over.o --workdir %t
// RUN: %python %S/../pm.py link --object %t/over.o --resident %t/p1 --recipe one_slot --output %t/over.elf --expect-rejected | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OVER
// OVER: refused: {{.*}}8224 bytes, larger than the 8192-byte slot
//
// Static constructors never run in an overlay: crt0 walks the constructor list
// once when the core starts, long before any overlay reaches the slot. The
// initializer here reads a volatile so the compiler cannot fold it away -- a
// constexpr-able one is evaluated at compile time and emits no constructor at
// all, which is a good way to write a test that passes for the wrong reason.
// RUN: %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR/bin/clang++ --target=aie2p-none-unknown-elf -O2 -c %S/ctor_overlay.cc -o %t/ctor.o
// RUN: %python %S/../pm.py link --object %t/ctor.o --resident %t/p1 --recipe one_slot --output %t/ctor.elf --expect-rejected | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CTOR
// CTOR: refused: {{.*}}has static constructors (.ctors)
// CTOR-SAME: {{.*}}
//
// Anything but .text has to live in *data* memory, which nothing swaps, so it
// would have to persist across every overlay simultaneously.
// RUN: %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR/bin/clang++ --target=aie2p-none-unknown-elf -O2 -c %S/rodata_overlay.cc -o %t/rodata.o
// RUN: %python %S/../pm.py link --object %t/rodata.o --resident %t/p1 --recipe one_slot --output %t/rodata.elf --expect-rejected | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RODATA
// RODATA: refused: {{.*}}expected exactly one allocatable section named .text
